  "rationale": "With no defences the attack succeeds: phish_workstation gives foothold_workstation and stolen_user. Then pivot_internal, auth_appserver, kerberoast_dc (stolen_admin), auth_dc, escalate_dc, dump_dbadmin_dc, auth_db, escalate_db and exfiltrate_db. So at least one control is needed. Every exfiltration path needs stolen_dbadmin, and only dump_dbadmin_dc and dump_dbadmin_adfs produce it. Those need admin_dc or admin_adfs, which need foothold_dc or foothold_adfs. The only ways to get those footholds are auth_dc and auth_adfs, and both require NOT mfa_admin. Deploying mfa:admin alone therefore blocks all paths to db, fileserver and backup, so exfiltration is impossible. Minimum = 1."
